<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Ms. Barton returns six weeks after sertraline was increased to 100 mg. At the nurse telephone check two weeks after the increase she reported three days of mild nausea and no restlessness or suicidal thoughts. She now has more good days than bad, enjoys her work again, and sleeps about six and a half hours. She has had ten CBT sessions and is using the sleep schedule. She increased to 35 hours a week after the last visit and this week to her new limit of 45 hours, and she has handed the families&apos; correspondence to a colleague. She has missed no doses and has had no side effects since the first few days after the increase. She has had no suicidal thoughts. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Interval change</td><td>More good days than bad; enjoying work again</td></tr><tr><td>Dose increase</td><td>Three days of mild nausea after the increase; nurse check at two weeks with no concerns</td></tr><tr><td>Sleep</td><td>About six and a half hours</td></tr><tr><td>Work</td><td>Up to 45 hours a week; correspondence delegated</td></tr><tr><td>Safety</td><td>No suicidal thoughts</td></tr><tr><td>PHQ-9</td><td>7, down from 18</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

