    <title>Assessment and Plan</title>
    <text><list listType="ordered"><item><content styleCode="Bold">Major depressive disorder, recurrent, responding (F33.1)</content>. PHQ-9 7, down 61 percent from 18: a response, not yet remission. GAD-7 4. Sleep at goal. Suicide risk remains low. [S]<list><item>Continue sertraline 100 mg.</item><item>Care-manager telephone PHQ-9 in about four weeks, then a review in two months.</item><item>Continue CBT to the end of the course.</item><item>Collaborative safety plan reviewed and unchanged; 988 Suicide &amp; Crisis Lifeline and the clinic number confirmed.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Occupational burnout (Z73.0)</content>. Back at full duties within the 45-hour limit. [S]<list><item>Keep the 45-hour limit; join the relief workers&apos; peer support group; no deployment for at least six months.</item></list></item></list><paragraph>Protocol monitoring: items the monitoring protocol calls for at this visit. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Domain</th><th>Measure</th><th>Interval</th><th>Status</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Survey</td><td>PHQ-9</td><td>Baseline, then at least monthly during acute treatment; every 2 to 4 weeks in continuation</td><td>Completed today</td><td>7, down 61 percent from 18: response; remission not yet reached</td></tr><tr><td>Survey</td><td>GAD-7</td><td>With the PHQ-9 when anxiety symptoms were present at baseline</td><td>Completed today</td><td>4, down from 9</td></tr><tr><td>Survey</td><td>Suicide risk reassessment (C-SSRS Since Last Visit and PHQ-9 item 9)</td><td>Every visit during active treatment</td><td>Completed today</td><td>No suicidal thoughts, intent, plan, or behavior since the last visit; PHQ-9 item 9 scored 0. Safety plan reviewed</td></tr><tr><td>Medication safety</td><td>Tolerability check two weeks after the dose increase</td><td>2 weeks after each dose change</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Done by nurse telephone call two weeks after the increase: three days of mild nausea, no activation or suicidal thoughts</td></tr><tr><td>Medication safety</td><td>Adherence and adverse-effect review</td><td>Every visit during active treatment</td><td>Completed today</td><td>No missed doses; no side effects now</td></tr><tr><td>Self-management</td><td>Psychotherapy, sleep, work hours, and social contact</td><td>Every visit during active treatment</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Ten CBT sessions; sleep about six and a half hours; 45-hour week; peer support group advised</td></tr><tr><td>Laboratory</td><td>Lithium, anticonvulsant, or antipsychotic monitoring (levels, metabolic tests, AIMS)</td><td>Only on those drugs</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>Treated with an SSRI only</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>Goal progress:</paragraph><list><item>Response (PHQ-9 down by at least 50 percent) by twelve weeks. Outcome by 2026-04-14: PHQ-9 7 at twelve weeks, down 61 percent from 18 [S]</item><item>Remission (PHQ-9 below 5) and continuation treatment for at least twelve months after remission. In progress; target 2026-06-16 [S]</item><item>Sleep at least six hours most nights. Outcome by 2026-04-14: About six and a half hours most nights by twelve weeks [S]</item><item>Phased return to work at no more than 45 hours a week, with no field deployment for at least six months. In progress; target 2026-06-16 [S]</item><item>Time with friends or her faith community at least twice a week. In progress; target 2026-06-16 [S]</item></list><paragraph>Guideline basis: VA/DoD Clinical Practice Guideline for the Management of Major Depressive Disorder (2022); VA/DoD Clinical Practice Guideline for Assessment and Management of Patients at Risk for Suicide (2024); CMID: Clinical Monitoring Intelligence Database, depression, bipolar, and mood disorders monograph (2026)</paragraph><paragraph>Follow-up: Care-manager telephone PHQ-9 in about four weeks; depression review in two months. Next scheduled visit 2026-06-16: five-month depression review in continuation treatment. [S]</paragraph></text>

  </section>
